st took my lunch."], [9.065, 12.78, "So for three years, I carried their bags to the dungeon door, and waited outside."], [12.992, 17.989, "Then my little sister got sick. The only cure grows on the bottom floor, and no party has ever made it that far."], [18.211, 20.46, "So I went in alone, with a lantern and a bread knife."], [20.683, 23.536, "Floor one. Forty goblins looked at me, and stepped aside."], [23.707, 25.591, "Floor five. A troll held the door."], [25.763, 27.393, "I didn't know why. I just kept walking."], [27.598, 31.939, "On the bottom floor sat the Dungeon King. He was as big as a church, and he was smiling."], [32.119, 39.258, "He said, \"A thousand years, they've come in fours and fives to kill me. You're the first one brave enough to come alone.\""], [39.317, 41.964, "He handed me the cure. Then he said, \"Is your party full?\""], [42.031, 43.897, "We walked out together. He carried my bag."], [44.108, 45.918, "Every party in town was standing at the door."], [46.104, 48.862, "The knight captain said, \"Kid. Got room for one more?\""], [49.044, 51.348, "I looked him up and down. \"Sorry. You're too small.\""], [51.573, 57.14, "Then the Dungeon King leaned down and whispered, \"There are six more dungeons. And their kings are lonely too.\""]]}